# Watch Wu-Tang Clan Perform the 2026 NFL Thanksgiving Day Halftime Show

> 🎵 *Curated Music Story from Pitchfork Official Publications*

### 📖 The Full Story

Newsletter Search Search News Reviews Best New Music Features Lists Columns Video Open Navigation Menu Menu Search Search News Watch Wu-Tang Clan Perform the 2026 NFL Thanksgiving Day Halftime Show The New York group took the stage in Detroit for the Bears vs. Lions football game By Nina Corcoran November 26, 2026 Wu-Tang Clan, Getty Images Comment Loader Save Story Save this story Comment Loader Save Story Save this story Fresh off their induction into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame mere days ago, Wu-Tang Clan stuck around the Midwest a little longer for a different celebration: performing at the NFL Thanksgiving Day halftime show at Detroit’s Ford Field, where the local Lions took on the Chicago Bears. Wu-Tang Clan opened with Wu-Tang Forever ’s “Triumph” in a medley that included “Protect Ya Neck,” “Bring Da Ruckus,” “C.R.E.A.M.,” and more. The famously New York-based hip-hop collective were sporting Lions gear for the big performance, while Red Hot Chili Peppers ’ Chad Smith joined them on drums in a Lions jersey as well. Watch videos from their set below.

This was the second halftime show performance at Ford Field under the Detroit Lions’ multi-year partnership with Eminem and Paul Rosenberg, the rapper’s longtime manager, during which they select the talent and serve as executive producers of the show. Last year, Eminem joined Jack White , both of who are proud Michigan natives, for the inaugural halftime show under his leadership.

When asked why they chose the New York City rap group to perform this year, Rosenberg explained that they were going for an element of surprise. “We often like to do things that are both exciting and unexpected. A Wu-Tang Clan Thanksgiving performance in Detroit certainly fits that description!” said Rosenberg. “Both Eminem and myself have been Wu fans since the early 90’s along with a whole generation of Detroit football fans. We are honored to bring them to this year’s stage.”

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

Wu-Tang Clan weren’t the only musicians invited to football games for the holiday. Last night (November 25), U2 got to play the inaugural Thanksgiving Eve halftime show at the Green Bay Packers vs. Los Angeles Rams game with a little help from the Womack Sisters. Later this evening, Miranda Lambert will perform at the halftime show during the Dallas Cowboys vs. Philadelphia Eagles game, too.

